{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "A Quiet Night at Home", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Feeling Nostalgic", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 13, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Subject and Object Relative Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>When you want to clarify which person or thing you are talking about, you use a relative clause.</p><p>You can begin a relative clause with <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for people, <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things or <span class=\"italic\">that</span> for either people or things.</p>You put the relative clause immediately after the noun it talks about.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A subject relative clause describes the subject of the clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "An object relative clause describes the object of the clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Relative Connector</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Type of Relative Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The consummate college rom-com that takes you back.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that takes you back\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The one who walked out on her!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who walked out on her\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She could never live up to his expectations, which were totally unreal.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"which were totally unreal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"which\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She runs into him at the coffee shop that he goes to all the time.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that he goes to all the time\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"object\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He finds out about the guy that she used to be with.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that she used to be with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"object\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Talking about Wishes and Imaginary Situations", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">wish</span> and the second conditional to talk about imaginary situations in the present or future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Wishes and sentences in the second conditional infer that what you want is probably not possible, or for some reason impossible.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Statement</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I wish it were all that easy!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"it's not that easy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If having it all were so easy, everyone would be happy.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"everyone is not happy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If college was actually like they showed it in the movies, it would be a snap!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"college is not like they show it in the movies\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I wish I could just go back for a few days and enjoy it all again.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I can't go back\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I wish I were young again like those kids in the movie!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I am not young like the kids in the movie\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "rom-com", "type": "name"}, {"content": "romantic comedy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love watching rom-coms!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about relationships.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "consummate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "perfect in every way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That was the consummate college rom-com!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to team up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to work together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They teamed up to get the work finished.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to run into", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to meet by accident", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She ran into him at the coffee shop.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to walk out on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to end a relationship", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He walked out her when she needed him!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to be a snap", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be easy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Making those cookies was a snap.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "crush", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a strong temporary attraction", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Didn't Peter have a crush on you, Vanessa?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to be up to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be doing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What are you up to this weekend?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to live up to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to meet a standard", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I could never live up to his expectations.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob09aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to take you back", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to bring back memories", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This movie takes me back to my college days.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob09aud10", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn7le13ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I do research on what college students did as social activities in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use the research to talk about wishes and imaginary situations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask a partner how they would feel about the past social situations.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Identify social activities college students do today. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find out what college students did in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look for past activities online, in the library, in old yearbooks at your school, or ask some older people.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the information to write about what you wish you could do and can't.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write what you would do if could.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write what you do actually do today.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your sentences to a partner and ask them how they feel about the activities.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about social activities.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about wishes and imaginary situations.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express complex statements using words like <span class=\"italic\">who</span>, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> or <span class=\"italic\">which</span>.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What m